  "live_records": {
    "q-36697": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36697",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {(\\pi /2)}^{+}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+x & \\text{ for }\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x<\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Approaching $x=0$ from the left, we have $x<0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡0 \\\\  & =2(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ from the right, we have $x>\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(\\pi /2)}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(\\pi /2)}^{+}}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
