    "q-302093": {
      "dom_id": "step-q302093",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the right-sided limit at $x=2$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}-16\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2x+5}-\\sqrt{2x}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Approaching from the right, we have $x>2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt{2x+5}-\\sqrt{2x}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(\\sqrt{2x+5}-\\sqrt{2x}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2\\cdot 2)+5}-\\sqrt{2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
